{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af163f3","nodeId":"4p5d3rzCHy4vjg2PRX-2k","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# Hot Reloading in Docker\n\nEven though we can speed up the image building with layer caching enable, we don't want to have to rebuild our container image with every code change. Instead, we want the state of our application in the container to reflect changes immediately. We can achieve this through a combination of bind mounts and hot reloading utilities!","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Hot Reloading - Docker","url":"https://courses.devopsdirective.com/docker-beginner-to-pro/lessons/11-development-workflow/01-hot-reloading","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbab6"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/4p5d3rzCHy4vjg2PRX-2k.md"}